# HTTP response headers for the static site.
#
# These cannot live in the page's <meta> CSP: browsers ignore frame-ancestors
# (and sandbox / report-uri) when the policy arrives in a meta element, so
# clickjacking protection has to be a real header. They also cannot live in
# worker/index.js — wrangler.jsonc sets run_worker_first: ["/api/*"], so page
# and asset requests are answered by Cloudflare's Asset Worker and never
# reach our fetch handler. This file is the mechanism that actually applies,
# and it keeps assets cacheable at the edge with no Worker invocation.
#
# The framing-only CSP here composes with each page's own meta CSP; CSP
# policies combine restrictively, so both apply.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), interest-cohort=()

/internal/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

# Fingerprinted assets: the filename changes whenever the bytes do
# (scripts/build-site.mjs), so the URL can be cached indefinitely. HTML keeps
# the default revalidate behaviour so a deploy is picked up immediately.
/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
